   "designUnitId": "lesson-section/starter/unit-001",
   "speakerNotes": "Teacher orientation: Children retrieve South America's place on a world map, learn what a biome is, notice the global tropical-rainforest pattern, then zoom in to locate and describe the Amazon from maps and real photographs. They produce a three-part description using biome, location and feature evidence. The tricky move is separating what a photograph can show about a biome from what a map can prove about location; this is taught in the final Teach beat and tested in Apply.\n\nSay to children: Start with the shape you know. Which continent is picked out? Now look at the water on its eastern side. Finally, which continent sits up and to the left? Keep those three places in mind. They'll help when we zoom in.\n\nAnswer to question(s) on this slide: South America; Atlantic Ocean; North America."
  },
